gates.prompt:
Implement a Node.js module from a structured ticket specification.

TICKET:
{{ticket_spec}}

REPO: {{target_dir}}
MODULE: {{module_name}}
REPO CONTEXT:
{{repo_context}}

Your task:
1. Analyze ticket: extract title, description, DONE-WHEN criteria
2. Review repo context: understand structure, conventions, patterns
3. Design and implement the module at lib/{{module_name}}.js
4. Create test file at test/{{module_name}}.test.js covering DONE-WHEN criteria
5. Write files using available tools

Return JSON: { "module_path": "lib/{{module_name}}.js", "test_path": "test/{{module_name}}.test.js", "files_created": [], "functions_exported": [], "implementation_notes": "", "done_when_coverage": [] }

Verify the module implementation meets all requirements.

TICKET DONE-WHEN:
{{ticket_spec}}

IMPLEMENTATION:
Files: {{module-implementer.files_created}}
Functions: {{module-implementer.functions_exported}}
Notes: {{module-implementer.implementation_notes}}

TEST RESULTS:
{{test_output}}

Return JSON: { "done_when_met": [{"criterion":"","status":"met|not_met|partial","evidence":""}], "test_status":"pass|fail", "test_failures":[], "code_quality_issues":[], "recommended_fixes":[], "verdict":"pass|fail", "summary":"" }
